TI  - Intermittent Aeration and Continuous Flow Biofilm Process for Treatment of Rural Domestic Sewage
AU  - HE Zong-jun
PY  - 2012
JO  - China Water & Wastewater
AB  - The intermittent aeration and continuous flow biofilm process was developed based on anaerobic treatment,three-stage aerobic/anoxic biofilm process and characteristics of rural domestic sewage.The actual treatment efficiency of the process was investigated.The actual treatment capacity was 48 m3/d,the HRT was 1.5 d,the hydraulic load in the hydrolysis acidification zone with media filling rate of 60% was 0.88 m3/(m3·d),and the hydraulic load in the contact oxidation zone with media filling rate of 75% was 4.57 m3/(m3·d).The operation results of six months showed that the average removal rates of COD,BOD5,NH3-N,TP and SS were 74.8%,83%,51.4%,60.3% and 81.8%,respectively,and the corresponding average effluent concentrations were below 57 mg/L,14.3 mg/L,19 mg/L,2.48 mg/L and 24 mg/L,respectively,meeting Integrated Wastewater Discharge Standard(DB 12/356-2008).The treated effluent could be used for irrigation.
