AU  - Institute of agroengineering and environmental problems of agricultural production – filial of the FGBNY FNATS VIM
PY  - 2025
JO  - Техника и технологии в животноводстве
VL  - 15
IS  - 1
DO  - 10.22314/27132064-2025-15-1-63
AB  - Currently, the agricultural production’s actual task is manure and dung utilization. The most modern technologies for manure (dung) disposal are processing in bioreactors, thermal drying, accelerated composting, and anaerobic digestion in methane tanks. Modern intensive processing methods are expensive and cannot be used for small agricultural enterprises and peasant (farming) facility, where long term storage and passive composting technologies are mainly used, having such disadvantages as long processing times, large nutrients losses, risk of leakage of polluted wastewater during the rainy season and spring floods increasing. As to these technology’s disadvantages eliminate, processing in an autonomous chamber-type biofermenter is proposed, to distinctive feature of which is the of solar panels as an alternative energy source using and a control unit allows this process of organic mixture processing in real time to control and monitor. A scheme for autonomous chamber-type biofermenter’s operation automating is proposed, taking into account the availability of equipment necessary for entire control system process: solar panels, a charge controller, rechargeable batteries, an inverter, a control unit, pressure and exhaust fans, temperature and oxygen concentration’s sensors, and a speed controller operating. The air supply to the biofermenter chamber is controlled taking into account the conditions of this mixture disinfection, while temperature and oxygen content in the mixture is a given range maintaining. A schematic diagram of measuring instruments (sensors) connecting to information recording devices is proposed, that transmission sequence of the signal received from temperature and differential pressure sensors to the reception unit ones indicating. These developments, aimed at biofermentation’s process automating in the real time, will improve the efficiency of organic waste in an autonomous biofermenter’s chamber-type processing.
